# Async action feedback

Any control that commits something (save, publish, restore, update password, etc.) must play the shared idle → pending → success (or failed) sequence. Do not swap the label to “Saving…” with no spinner, and do not skip success just because the request was fast.

## Use these primitives

- Timing: `useSaveFeedback` in `~/hooks/use-save-feedback`
- Button content: `SaveFeedbackLabel` in `~/app/_components/save-feedback-label`
- Motion: `SAVE_FEEDBACK_CONTENT_TRANSITION` (`duration: 0.18`, ease `[0.22, 1, 0.36, 1]`). Previous content fades out; the next state fades and slides in from `y: -6`.

Do not invent a second spinner, check icon, or Framer transition for this.

## Timing

| Token | Value | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `SAVE_FEEDBACK_MIN_SAVING_MS` | 500 | Minimum spinner time, even if the server returns instantly |
| `SAVE_FEEDBACK_RESULT_MS` | 1200 | How long Saved / Failed stays before idle |
| `SAVE_FEEDBACK_SETTLE_MS` | 700 | Delay before close, navigate, or removing the row |

`start()` before the request. `await settle("saved" | "failed")` after. Use `runAfterResult` (or an equivalent timeout) for navigation/list updates so success is visible first.

## Button

- Idle / pending / success labels (e.g. Restore → Restoring → Restored)
- Spinner (`Loader2`) while pending; check (`Check`) on success
- Keep contrast while feedback plays: `disabled:opacity-100`
- Errors: toast is fine; the button may return to idle (or `failedLabel`)

```tsx
feedback.start();
const ok = await doThing();
await feedback.settle(ok ? "saved" : "failed");
if (ok) {
  window.setTimeout(reveal, SAVE_FEEDBACK_SETTLE_MS);
}

<SaveFeedbackLabel
  state={feedback.state}
  idleLabel="Restore"
  savingLabel="Restoring"
  savedLabel="Restored"
/>
```

